<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue id="40b8-2e24-0115-9ee6" name="Gauls" revision="5" battleScribeVersion="2.03" authorName="Jono Firth" authorUrl="https://www.greatescapegames.co.uk/uploads/images/wysiwyg/home-shortcuts/coe/earlyclassical/Gallic_May_25th_2011.pdf" library="false" gameSystemId="c749-87c2-0d4a-5e29" gameSystemRevision="12" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <readme>‘The Gauls are tall of body, with rippling muscles, and white of skin. Their hair is fair, not only by nature but also because of their custom of accentuating it by artificial means. They wash their hair in lime water then pull it back so that it resembles a horse’s mane. Some of them shave their beard, others let it grow. The nobles shave their cheeks but let their moustache grow until it covers their mouth.’ - Diodorus Siculus

A Gallic army must include a warlord or chieftain and at least two warband units. Enemies included the Early Romans, Etruscans, Samnites, Republican Romans, Carthaginians, Ancient Spanish, Ancient Germans, Dacians, Thracians, Illyrians and other Gauls.</readme>
  <categoryEntries>
    <categoryEntry id="d8c9-28dd-2ef7-5d52" name="Gallic" hidden="false"/>
  </categoryEntries>
